<title>TUNISIA: Tunisian expatriates remit 754 mln dinars in 1996.</title>
<headline>Tunisian expatriates remit 754 mln dinars in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Remittances by Tunisians living abroad amounted to 754 million dinars ($684 million) in 1996, up from 687 million dinars in 1995, Central Bank statistics showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>There are 610,000 Tunisian emigrants living abroad, 75 percent of them in western Europe, mainly in France where they number more than 344,000, official figures show.</p>
<p>Workers' remittances are the second most important source of Tunisia's net income in foreign currency after tourism. ($=0.1.1025 dinar)</p>
<p>Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
